(300131, 21302, 3087, '<td valign="top">I really like this - it reminds me of the sun motifs which were common on front doors - I think in the 1930s or 1940s. I remember studying them at school - briefly, as part of some other subject. The tupperware registered trademark ties in with that era too. The colour is wonderful and I love the dark and light shadows. I''d like to crop this a little so that the "sun" was positioned on a vertical and horizonal thirds intersection point.</td>', 'I really like this - it reminds me of the sun motifs which were common on front doors - I think in the 1930s or 1940s. I remember studying them at school - briefly, as part of some other subject. The tupperware registered trademark ties in with that era too. The colour is wonderful and I love the dark and light shadows. I''d like to crop this a little so that the "sun" was positioned on a vertical and horizonal thirds intersection point.', '2003-05-16 12:03:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(300139, 21249, 5112, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo!  Love the colours (how can you go wrong with warm orange tones).  The greys of the stones/cement set of the oranges beautifully.  To my eyes, the picture looks slightly "curved" to the top, as if the building weren''t entirely straight (might be the bifocals); you couldn''t get a tall ladder to stand on when taking the picture?  Just kidding.  So, they use plastic shopping bags there also? ~9</td>', 'Beautiful photo!  Love the colours (how can you go wrong with warm orange tones).  The greys of the stones/cement set of the oranges beautifully.  To my eyes, the picture looks slightly "curved" to the top, as if the building weren''t entirely straight (might be the bifocals); you couldn''t get a tall ladder to stand on when taking the picture?  Just kidding.  So, they use plastic shopping bags there also? ~9', '2003-05-16 12:15:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(300141, 21418, 5112, '<td valign="top">San Francisco?  Love the moon in the sky!</td>', 'San Francisco?  Love the moon in the sky!', '2003-05-16 12:16:51.000000', NULL, 1),
